/// REPRO (iterators vertical, 2026-07-15) — a `@test` (or any component-boundary export) whose name
/// has a KEBAB SEGMENT STARTING WITH A DIGIT silently breaks the ENTIRE test component: every test in
/// the file reports FAIL with NO diagnostic, not just the offending one. `cdz check` PASSES.
///
/// ROOT: WIT kebab-case requires each hyphen-delimited label to start with an ASCII LETTER (`a-z`).
/// rcdzc emits a `@test` def's name verbatim as a component export name without validating it, so a
/// name like `range-step-by-2` / `step-2` / `a-2-b` produces an INVALID component, which wasmtime
/// rejects wholesale — surfacing as "0 passed, N failed" with no explanation (the same silent-reject
/// class as the general kebab-extern-name gotcha).
///
/// DISCRIMINATORS (all verified):
///   - `step2` (digit INSIDE a word segment)      → OK, compiles + runs.
///   - `range-step-by-two` (all-letter segments)  → OK.
///   - `step-2`, `a-2-b`, `range-step-2x`, `range-step-by-2` (a segment STARTS with a digit) → BREAK.
///   - The break takes down the WHOLE component: unrelated passing tests in the same file all FAIL.
///
/// EXPECTED: either accept the name (mangle the emitted label to a valid kebab form) or REJECT it at
/// check-time with a clear diagnostic ("a test/export name segment must start with a letter: `-2`"),
/// never a silent total-component failure.
///
/// This file is a DEMONSTRATION: `cdz test` on it yields "0 passed, 2 failed" purely because of the
/// numeric-segment name — flip `step-by-2` to `step-by-two` and BOTH pass.

def double(n) = n * 2

@test
def step-by-2() =
  // this test's own logic is trivially true; it FAILS only because its NAME has a numeric kebab segment
  if double(3) == 6 then unit else trap("double 3 is 6")

@test
def an-unrelated-passing-test() =
  // correct + independent, yet it ALSO reports FAIL — collateral damage from the invalid component
  if double(10) == 20 then unit else trap("double 10 is 20")

/// RESOLVED 2026-07-15 (trunk@dd77ccc1b): a digit-led kebab segment in an export/@test name now REJECTS with CDZ0201 + a fix-it (rename to letter-led segments) instead of silently failing the whole component.
